{%- comment -%}
  Renders the chevron icon.

  Source: phase-3-assets/icons/icon-chevron.svg, drawn in Phase 3 — 24x24
  canvas, stroke 1.5, currentColor, round caps and joins. Drawn pointing right;
  it is rotated rather than redrawn, which is why only one chevron exists in
  the set.

  Round, not square. Phase 2 §18.3 rule 2 specifies square caps and mitred
  joins; every glyph Phase 3 drew and Phases 4-7 shipped uses round ones, so
  matching the set is what keeps the icons looking like one drawing. The
  deviation belongs to the set, not to this file, and is recorded in
  PHASE-8-PRODUCT-SHOPPING-UX.md rather than half-corrected here.

  Accepts:
  - class: {String} optional extra class names. The rotation is owned by the
    control the chevron sits in — sections/main-product.liquid's disclosure
    rotates it from .main-product__details-summary — rather than by a modifier
    class here, so there is one rule per consumer and no unused class.

  Usage:
  {% render 'icon-chevron' %}

  Decorative: the control it sits in carries the accessible name and, for a
  disclosure, the open state.
{%- endcomment -%}
<svg class="icon icon--chevron {{ class }}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9.5 5.5 16 12l-6.5 6.5"/></svg>
